1
00:03:44,444 --> 00:03:50,444
Nothing in this world has prepared you for this.

2
00:07:28,888 --> 00:07:34,888
Mortal Kombat is a action, fantasy film directed by Paul W. S. Anderson.

3
00:11:13,333 --> 00:11:19,333
For nine generations an evil sorcerer has been victorious in
hand-to-hand battle against his mortal enemies.

4
00:14:57,777 --> 00:15:03,777
If he wins a tenth Mortal Kombat tournament, desolation and
evil will reign over the multiverse forever.

5
00:18:42,222 --> 00:18:48,222
To save Earth, three warriors must overcome seemingly insurmountable
odds, their own inner demons, and superhuman foes.

6
00:22:26,666 --> 00:22:32,666
Liu Kang, played by Robin Shou.

7
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:17,111
Johnny Cage, played by Linden Ashby.

8
00:29:55,555 --> 00:30:01,555
Sonya Blade, played by Bridgette Wilson-Sampras.

9
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Lord Raiden, played by Christopher Lambert.

10
00:37:24,444 --> 00:37:30,444
Shang Tsung, played by Cary-Hiroyuki Tagawa.

11
00:41:08,888 --> 00:41:14,888
Princess Kitana, played by Talisa Soto.

12
00:44:53,333 --> 00:44:59,333
Mortal Kombat is a 1995 American martial arts fantasy film based on
the video game franchise by Ed Boon and John Tobias.

13
00:48:37,777 --> 00:48:43,777
It is the first installment in the Mortal Kombat film series.

14
00:52:22,222 --> 00:52:28,222
It was directed by Paul Anderson and stars Linden Ashby, Cary-Hiroyuki Tagawa,
Robin Shou, Bridgette Wilson, Talisa Soto, and Christopher Lambert.

15
00:56:06,666 --> 00:56:12,666
The film follows a group of heroes who participate in the eponymous tournament
to protect Earth from being conquered by malevolent forces.

16
00:59:51,111 --> 00:59:57,111
Its story primarily adapts the original 1992 game, while also
using elements from the game Mortal Kombat II (1993).

17
01:03:35,555 --> 01:03:41,555
Development of a Mortal Kombat film adaptation began shortly after the release of Mortal Kombat II
when independent producer Lawrence Kasanoff acquired the rights from Midway Games.

18
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:26,000
Newcomer director Anderson was hired based on the strength of his debut
Shopping, with a screenplay written by Kevin Droney.

19
01:11:04,444 --> 01:11:10,444
Filming took place primarily in Thailand, with fight
sequences supervised by Shou and Pat E.

20
01:14:48,888 --> 01:14:54,888
Mortal Kombat premiered in the United States on August 18, 1995.

21
01:18:33,333 --> 01:18:39,333
It received mixed reviews from critics, who praised the martial art sequences, atmosphere, and production
values, but criticized the performances, script, and toned-down violence from the games.

22
01:22:17,777 --> 01:22:23,777
Despite the mixed critical response, the film was
well received by fans of the series.

23
01:26:02,222 --> 01:26:08,222
It was also a commercial success, grossing $122.2
million on a $20 million budget.

24
01:29:46,666 --> 01:29:52,666
The film was followed by a 1997 sequel, Mortal Kombat Annihilation, along with two television series: the animated sequel
Mortal Kombat: Defenders of the Realm (1996) and the live-action prequel Mortal Kombat: Conquest (1998–1999).

25
01:33:31,111 --> 01:33:37,111
The follow-ups were unable to match the original film's success
and the series was rebooted with a 2021 film.

26
01:37:15,555 --> 01:37:21,555
The film explores themes of island, martial arts,
monster, saving the world, magic.
